---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { DOCKER_COMPOSE_SNIPPET, DOCKER_RUN_SNIPPET } from '../lib/config';
import { NAV, SITE } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base
  title="Self-Host Quick Start"
  description="Deploy itemized with Docker Compose, Docker Run, or Unraid Community Apps, and configure HTTPS for mobile barcode scanning."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">Self-Host</p>
      <h1>Up and running in one container.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Pre-built multi-architecture images (<code>linux/amd64</code> and <code>linux/arm64</code>) are published to GitHub Container Registry at <code>{SITE.image}</code>.
      </p>
      <nav class="jump-nav" aria-label="Deployment methods">
        <a href="#docker-compose">Docker Compose</a>
        <a href="#docker-run">Docker Run</a>
        <a href="#unraid">Unraid</a>
        <a href="#https">HTTPS &amp; Reverse Proxy</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section" id="docker-compose" aria-labelledby="compose-title">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="kicker">Recommended</p>
      <h2 id="compose-title">Docker Compose</h2>
      <p>
        Create a <code>docker-compose.yml</code> file and mount a persistent volume at <code>/data</code> where itemized stores its SQLite WAL database (<code>/data/itemized.db</code>).
      </p>
      <CodeBlock label="docker-compose.yml" code={DOCKER_COMPOSE_SNIPPET} />
      <CodeBlock label="Start the container" code="docker compose up -d" />
      <p>
        Open <code>http://localhost:8080</code> (or your reverse-proxy HTTPS URL) in a browser to complete first-run administrator setup.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt" id="docker-run" aria-labelledby="run-title">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="kicker">Single command</p>
      <h2 id="run-title">Docker Run</h2>
      <p>
        Prefer running Docker directly? Pass the same port, volume, and environment variables via <code>docker run</code>:
      </p>
      <CodeBlock label="Shell" code={DOCKER_RUN_SNIPPET} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="unraid" aria-labelledby="unraid-title">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="kicker">Unraid</p>
      <h2 id="unraid-title">Unraid Community Apps</h2>
      <p>
        An official Unraid template is maintained in the repository at <a href={SITE.unraidTemplate}><code>unraid/itemized.xml</code></a>.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Automatic <code>/data</code> ownership:</strong> The container entrypoint ensures <code>/data</code> matches <code>PUID:PGID</code> (<code>99:100</code> / <code>nobody:users</code> in the Unraid template, or <code>1000:1000</code> by default) before dropping privileges to run <code>/usr/local/bin/itemized</code> as a non-root user.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Explicit <code>--user</code> support:</strong> If launched with an explicit non-root <code>--user</code> flag, privilege dropping is skipped automatically.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Direct LAN printer access:</strong> Standard bridge networking reaches LAN printers directly on outbound connections, supporting both Zebra ZSB IPP endpoints (<code>:631</code>) and Raw TCP ZPL printers (<code>:9100</code>).
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt" id="https" aria-labelledby="https-title">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="kicker">Required for mobile scanning</p>
      <h2 id="https-title">HTTPS &amp; Reverse Proxy</h2>
      <div class="callout callout-warn">
        <p>
          <strong>Mobile browsers require HTTPS for live camera access.</strong> Modern mobile browsers (including iOS Safari and Chrome or Firefox on iOS) disable the camera API (<code>navigator.mediaDevices</code>) on plain <code>http://</code> LAN URLs such as <code>http://192.168.1.x:8080</code>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p>
        To use live camera barcode scanning on phones and tablets, serve itemized over <strong>HTTPS</strong> behind a reverse proxy such as <strong>Nginx Proxy Manager</strong>, <strong>Caddy</strong>, <strong>Traefik</strong>, <strong>SWAG</strong>, or <strong>Tailscale Serve</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>When running behind a reverse proxy, configure two environment variables:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><code>TRUST_PROXY=true</code>: ensures rate limiting reads client IP addresses from <code>X-Forwarded-For</code> / <code>X-Real-IP</code>.</li>
        <li><code>BASE_URL=https://itemized.example.com</code>: ensures printed QR labels encode your HTTPS address.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="cta-row" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={NAV.configuration}>
          <span>Configuration &amp; Printing Reference</span>
          <Icon name="arrow-right" size={16} />
        </a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href={NAV.install}>Install Mobile PWA</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
